{"seq":46,"runId":"brownfield-live","at":"2026-10-29T16:11:25.913182Z","event":{"type":"DecisionRecorded","nodeId":"design","title":"Asynchronous Click Recording","choice":"Implement click recording asynchronously using Spring's `@Async` with a `ThreadPoolTaskExecutor` configured with a bounded queue.","rationale":"This choice directly addresses NFR-1 by decoupling click recording from the critical redirect path, ensuring minimal latency impact on redirects. A `ThreadPoolTaskExecutor` with a bounded queue prevents unbounded memory growth under high load, aligning with the 'best effort' principle for analytics data. If the queue is full, the click event will be logged as an error and dropped, prioritizing redirect performance over analytics completeness.","alternatives":["Synchronous recording: Rejected due to NFR-1 (performance impact).","External Message Queue (e.g., Kafka, RabbitMQ): Rejected for simplicity and added operational overhead for basic analytics. While more robust for high-volume, guaranteed delivery, it's considered overkill for the current requirements and 'best effort' nature."],"basedOn":["requirements.spec@v1#2c89879a220c","impact.analysis@v1#1209a53b2ab7"]},"prevHash":"4ec4b5ff8d1272e6a4b611b9c05cf2787e8be1aa7e3dfcf4dc45234b78a65048","hash":"11a3c72ea8f810f046e7a5f21cb0b53ebd7b95457191678cb525d746b8694b94"}
{"seq":47,"runId":"brownfield-live","at":"2026-10-29T16:11:25.913432Z","event":{"type":"DecisionRecorded","nodeId":"design","title":"User-Agent Parsing Library","choice":"Use the `ua-parser-java` library for determining the coarse user-agent family.","rationale":"This choice addresses Q-2 by providing a well-maintained, lightweight solution for user-agent classification. It reduces custom regex complexity and improves accuracy compared to simpler heuristics, ensuring reasonable accuracy and maintainability.","alternatives":["Custom regex-based logic: Rejected due to complexity, maintenance burden, and potential for inaccuracies as user-agent strings evolve.","Simpler heuristics (e.g., checking for 'bot' substring): Rejected as it would be less accurate and robust than a dedicated library."],"basedOn":["requirements.spec@v1#2c89879a220c","impact.analysis@v1#1209a53b2ab7"]},"prevHash":"11a3c72ea8f810f046e7a5f21cb0b53ebd7b95457191678cb525d746b8694b94","hash":"cdd21acf4f4a49795afe44cb2787fcf23729e9d045c509e7021799a8cff7b67f"}
{"seq":48,"runId":"brownfield-live","at":"2026-10-29T16:11:25.913550Z","event":{"type":"DecisionRecorded","nodeId":"design","title":"Expired Link Handling with Cache","choice":"Modify `LinkResolver` to store full `Link` objects (containing `expiresAt`) in the Caffeine cache. On every `resolve` call, explicitly check the `expiresAt` field of the cached `Link` object against the current time.","rationale":"This choice directly addresses FR-3 and NFR-4 by ensuring that expired links consistently return HTTP 410 Gone, even when present in the cache. It centralizes the expiration logic within the `LinkResolver`, making it robust and easy to reason about. The existing `Cache-Control: no-store` header on redirects means browsers won't cache the redirect itself, but the service's internal cache still needs this explicit check.","alternatives":["Cache-aside with TTL matching `expiresAt`: Rejected because `expiresAt` can be dynamic and setting individual TTLs for each cache entry based on `expiresAt` can be complex and less reliable than an explicit check, especially if `expiresAt` is updated or is null (never expires).","Proactive cache invalidation on expiry: Rejected due to complexity. Requires a background job to scan for expired links and invalidate cache entries, which adds latency to the 410 response (NFR-4 requires within 1 minute) and introduces potential race conditions. An explicit check is simpler and more reliable."],"basedOn":["requirements.spec@v1#2c89879a220c","impact.analysis@v1#1209a53b2ab7"]},"prevHash":"cdd21acf4f4a49795afe44cb2787fcf23729e9d045c509e7021799a8cff7b67f","hash":"2c6c7b9c41e0ac1f568859f530148a3f67b1f0a7552b43e21158f5d0f30d4f37"}
{"seq":49,"runId":"brownfield-live","at":"2026-10-29T16:11:25.913682Z","event":{"type":"DecisionRecorded","nodeId":"design","title":"Daily Click Count Time Zone","choice":"Aggregate daily click counts using UTC for daily boundaries.","rationale":"This choice addresses Q-4 by providing a consistent, unambiguous global standard for time-series data. It simplifies analysis and avoids issues with daylight saving changes or server time zone configurations, ensuring data integrity and ease of interpretation.","alternatives":["Server's local time zone: Rejected due to inconsistency across different deployment environments and potential for confusion with daylight saving.","Client's requested time zone: Rejected due to added complexity for the API (requiring a time zone header) and potential for inconsistent data if different clients request different time zones."],"basedOn":["requirements.spec@v1#2c89879a220c","impact.analysis@v1#1209a53b2ab7"]},"prevHash":"2c6c7b9c41e0ac1f568859f530148a3f67b1f0a7552b43e21158f5d0f30d4f37","hash":"e4712f9ca7984abe89d12b82da877c5f907606a77eb3feb7a519b740b24831a5"}
{"seq":50,"runId":"brownfield-live","at":"2026-10-29T16:11:25.913798Z","event":{"type":"DecisionRecorded","nodeId":"design","title":"Click Data Retention","choice":"Store raw click events in the `clicks` table indefinitely for now, but monitor storage growth. If storage becomes an issue, implement a policy to archive or purge raw click records older than 90 days, while retaining aggregated daily counts for longer periods (e.g., 1 year or indefinitely).","rationale":"This choice balances the immediate need for detailed analytics with potential future storage cost concerns (Risk: Storage cost increase). NFR-3 only requires 7 days of *daily counts*, not raw clicks. This approach provides flexibility to adapt to future analytical requirements while having a plan for managing data volume.","alternatives":["No retention policy: Rejected as it leads to unbounded storage growth and potential performance degradation over time.","Immediate aggregation and discard of raw clicks: Rejected as it limits future analytical capabilities (e.g., hourly trends, specific referrer analysis beyond host) if requirements evolve."],"basedOn":["requirements.spec@v1#2c89879a220c","impact.analysis@v1#1209a53b2ab7"]},"prevHash":"e4712f9ca7984abe89d12b82da877c5f907606a77eb3feb7a519b740b24831a5","hash":"4b2ee47e7db9cc776c86590b00d5a45d98d476f923cb43fd8101571bb5bc287b"}
